  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Saturday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Southerly winds intensify across much of\nthe region today as storm systems approach from the NW and SW.\nStrongest winds will be across portions of east-central Nevada\n(including NE Nye, White Pine and portions of SE Elko Counties)\nwhere S-SW winds of 15 to 30 mph and gusts of 35 to 50 mph are \nexpected. Blowing dust and reduced visibilities are a concern \nthis afternoon as conditions have been dry for quite some time. \nWinds will weaken overnight into Sunday, with another round of \ngusty S-SW winds Sunday afternoon and evening in these same \nlocations. Weak instability will set up across portions of eastern\nNevada this afternoon, with a 25% chance of thunderstorms for \ngenerally the eastern two-thirds of Elko County and most of White\nPine County. The strong surge of moisture coming up from southern\nNV will begin to impact east-central Nevada around or shortly \nafter midnight tonight, with moderate to heavy rainfall expanding\nwest and north Sunday into Sunday night. Sunday afternoon there\nwill also be a 20% chance of thunderstorms across most of central\nand northeastern Nevada. With the exception of Humboldt County, \nmost of the CWA is expected to receive at least a half inch of \nrainfall between 5AM Sunday and 5AM Monday. Heaviest rains are \nstill expected across east-central Nevada where an inch to an \ninch and a half of storm-total rainfall amounts are forecast. By\nMonday evening the system will be centered over southern CA, then\neject eastward through southern NV and into the four corners \nregion by late Tuesday. Lighter rain showers are expected to \ncontinue over most of northern and central Nevada Monday night \ninto Tuesday morning with showers ending from west to east Tuesday\nafternoon and overnight. Dry but noticeably cooler conditions are\nexpected Wednesday through at least next Friday. \n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High forecast confidence \nregarding strong wind gusts in Central Nevada this afternoon and\nevening, with moderate confidence in strong winds Sunday. High \nforecast confidence regarding significant rainfall in Eastern \nNevada Sunday into Monday. High forecast confidence in a cooling \ntrend through Monday.",
